## Calculation rules

- Scheduled duration is separate from paid hours.
- Do not assume unpaid breaks.
- Calculate weekly scheduled totals from actual assignments.
- Attribute the full scheduled duration to the assignment’s start date for weekly totals.
- Calculate rest using full start/end dates and times.
- Night assignments belong to their starting date.
- Show “Next day” beside the Night end time.
- Show the full following-day end date in detailed views.
- Carry Night coverage across midnight.
- Day/Swing overlap is 12:30–16:30.
- General coverage is 09:00–18:00.
- Mark operational boundaries at 07:30, 12:30, 16:30, and 20:30.
- Include General markers at 09:00 and 18:00.
- Show scheduled handovers separately from shift boundaries.
- Use 30-minute coverage resolution where needed.

Calculate coverage using actual timestamp intervals. Treat intervals as start-inclusive and end-exclusive so adjacent assignments are not double-counted at an exact boundary.

Count staffed positions using eligible assignments mapped to positions. Do not count one operator as filling two simultaneous positions or count one position twice.

Seed sufficient assignments before and after both the reporting week and planning week to validate rest and overnight coverage at their boundaries.

